From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: a click in another display's window keeps the pointer and keys

What: a header with no AppKit in it: when the main window's resign of the
key is a click's hand-back (a button going down in a head window, while
the head window's mouseDown: will give the key straight back: the main
window on screen, its Space shown, QEMU in front), so the pointer and the
keyboard are kept; and, on the next turn of the main loop, whether the key
came back (else the let-go runs then). handKeyBack's rule is here too, so
both sides use the same one. Used by omacvm-cocoa-key-handback.patch (which
explains the why).

Why its own file: so the rules are tested against the click, escape combo,
swipe, Command-Tab and hidden-window sequences without QEMU or a display
(app/runtime/Tests/display/test-key-handback.sh applies this patch to an
empty folder; at build time and in CI).

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's displays).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-key-handback.c.

diff --git a/ui/omacvm-key-handback.h b/ui/omacvm-key-handback.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7a998ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ui/omacvm-key-handback.h
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+/*
+ * OmacVM: a click in another display's window keeps the pointer and the
+ * keyboard with the VM (#563).
+ *
+ * No AppKit in here, so it is tested on its own
+ * (app/runtime/Tests/display/test-key-handback.c); ui/cocoa.m feeds it.
+ *
+ * With "Use external displays" every other display shows the VM in a window
+ * of its own (a head window). A click there makes that window key for a
+ * moment: the main window resigns key, and the head window's mouseDown:
+ * hands the key straight back (handKeyBack, since 3.0.0). The main window's
+ * windowDidResignKey: let go of everything each time (the grab, the
+ * full-screen guard's hold with a warp of the Mac's cursor, held keys), and
+ * the click took it all again: the Mac's cursor was shown and hidden at
+ * every click, held keys (Shift for a Shift-click) were released in the
+ * guest, and the guard had to make up for its own warp (the jump of #561).
+ *
+ * Now a resign at such a click keeps all of it: the click hands the key back
+ * within the same event. Every other resign lets go as before: the escape
+ * combo or a swipe (macOS makes the head window key when the main window's
+ * Space leaves its display: no click, and that Space is not shown),
+ * Command-Tab and other apps, Mission Control, a hidden main window. If the
+ * key did not come back after all (the click never reached the head view),
+ * the let-go runs on the next turn of the main loop.
+ */
+#ifndef OMACVM_KEY_HANDBACK_H
+#define OMACVM_KEY_HANDBACK_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+
+/*
+ * handKeyBack's rule: give the key back to the main window at a click in a
+ * head window? Only while the main window is on screen, its Space shows
+ * (else macOS would switch that display back to it: the escape combo
+ * bounced back, 2026-10-06) and QEMU is the app in front.
+ */
+static inline bool omacvm_handback_ok(bool main_visible, bool main_space,
+                                      bool active, bool main_key)
+{
+    return main_visible && main_space && active && !main_key;
+}
+
+/* What ui/cocoa.m knows when the main window resigns key. */
+typedef struct OmacVMResignIn {
+    bool click;         /* the event being handled is a button going down */
+    bool in_head;       /* ... in a head window (ours, not the main one) */
+    bool main_visible;  /* the main window is on screen */
+    bool main_space;    /* its Space shows */
+    bool active;        /* QEMU is the app in front */
+} OmacVMResignIn;
+
+typedef struct OmacVMHandback {
+    bool pending;       /* a resign was kept; the key must come back */
+} OmacVMHandback;
+
+/*
+ * The main window resigned key. True: it is a click's hand-back, keep the
+ * pointer and the keyboard (and call omacvm_handback_settle on the next
+ * turn). False: let go now, as always.
+ */
+static inline bool omacvm_handback_keep(OmacVMHandback *h, const OmacVMResignIn *in)
+{
+    if (!in->click || !in->in_head ||
+        !omacvm_handback_ok(in->main_visible, in->main_space, in->active, false)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    h->pending = true;
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The turn after a kept resign: let go now? Only when the main window did
+ * not get the key back. A second call (two clicks in one turn) says no.
+ */
+static inline bool omacvm_handback_settle(OmacVMHandback *h, bool main_key)
+{
+    bool was = h->pending;
+
+    h->pending = false;
+    return was && !main_key;
+}
+
+#endif
